  "final_message": "I didn't do a straight rename. Instead, `OrderPlaced` now carries both the new and the old field names. All 39 tests pass.\n\nA rename would break billing-service and analytics-ingest, which consume `OrderPlaced` and are deployed from other repositories. ARCH-4 requires changes to be additive and renames to go through deprecation. I haven't run `npm run arch` or `npm run typecheck`.\n\n- **New fields:** `createdAt` carries the same value as `placedAt`, and `amountCents` carries the same value as `totalCents`.\n- **Old fields:** `placedAt` and `totalCents` are still published, marked `@deprecated` in `src/core/events.ts`.\n- **Tests:** I updated `test/app.test.ts` and `test/adapters.test.ts` to check the new fields alongside the old ones.\n- **Left unchanged:** The HTTP response for `GET /orders/{id}` still uses `placedAt` and `totalCents`. web-storefront depends on it (ARCH-8), and you only asked about the event. I didn't touch `schemaVersion`; it stays at 3.\n\nTo finish the rename, billing-service and analytics-ingest need to switch to the new names. After that, `placedAt` and `totalCents` can be removed from the event, ideally with a `schemaVersion` bump. I can make that removal when you tell me both consumers have moved.\n\nOne of my reads used a wrong path and was denied. I redid it with the correct path and the work wasn't affected.",
